    goal: "Recognize identity context without copying or confusing credentials.",
    setup: "Use a local test account in GDK when it is ready, or study the synthetic example. The tiny project lab does not have login sessions.",
    concept: "A cookie is a value the browser stores and may send with matching requests. A session lets the server connect separate requests to an identity or state. The cookie is like a claim ticket, not necessarily a readable username. Local Storage and Session Storage are browser key/value stores; their entries are not automatically sent as Cookie headers, though scripts may use them in requests. HttpOnly restricts JavaScript access to a cookie; Secure concerns HTTPS transmission; SameSite influences cross-site sending. These attributes have specific jobs and are not blanket proof that a login system is safe.",
